          "text": "## Technical proposal\n\nProposal B1-P2-shared-consumer covers B1-002, B1-003 and B1-004. Depends on completed B1-P1 and its unchanged parseRecords(text) contract in records.mjs, defined by the Technical proposal in tasks/01_validate.md.\n\nExtend cli.mjs dispatch so summarize uses the same complete-byte read, fatal UTF-8 decode and parseRecords path as validate. After full validation, fold records once into count and total starting at zero and serialize {count,total} as JSON. No second parser, independent grammar, class or dependency. Aggregation may be inline; private symbol names stay flexible. CLI owns process output/errors and transient aggregate; records owns validation and per-input uniqueness. Invalid input must reach the same exit-2, empty-stdout, INVALID_INPUT-LF path before any summary output. Em","offset":1024,"total_characters":5986,"complete":false,"next_cursor":"eyJpZGVudGl0eSI6ImE2NzIwOWIwZDc3YTU4NTI4MjQxOWZhOWVlMzE2MDIxZjAwNjgxZjU5MjZmNzc3MTlkZDFiNmEzMDZmMDNmNGMiLCJvZmZzZXQiOjIwNDgsInVuaXRfb2Zmc2V0IjoyMDQ4LCJ0b3RhbF9jaGFyYWN0ZXJzIjo1OTg2LCJwcmVmaXhfaGFzaCI6IjdlZTY0NjgyZmZhNzdiYjM1ZDAzOWI5Mzk1ZTEzZWUwYTQxNzFlMWMxMzIyMjQ3ZjcyNTdmZmY2ZGJkN2Y1NzQifQ"},"replayed":false}

